 "story": "Calm, one hand resting on her bump, her thumb stroking it. Something's not right \u2014 a small intake, her fingers press in, she swallows and her eyes drop. Then the nausea comes: her hand lifts in front of her and covers her mouth as her eyes squeeze shut; her throat clenches and she retches \u2014 a sharp hit, a release, a smaller second one \u2014 her other hand grabbing her cardigan; she rides it out with two slow, controlled breaths through her hand; it passes \u2014 her hand peels away and falls back to her bump with a long sigh, and she softens, looking down at it with relief.",
